# Bump version on every commit

Whenever you create a git commit in this repo, bump the patch version in the same commit (1.0.6 → 1.0.7, and so on). Do this even if the user only said “commit” or “push”.

`apps/web/package.json` `version` is the source of truth (Vite stamps it into the UI and the service worker cache). Keep these in lockstep:

- `apps/web/package.json`
- `apps/api/package.json`
- root `package.json`
- the matching `version` fields for those packages in `package-lock.json` and `apps/web/package-lock.json`

Do not change dependency versions (for example `content-type`). Skip the bump only if the commit is already a version-only bump with no other changes.
